  ISSN={0006-8950}, 
  url={https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6202576/}, 
  DOI={10.1093/brain/awy273}, 
  abstractNote={On the 150th anniversary of Korbinian Brodmann’s birth, and the 100th anniversary of his death, Zilles celebrates his pioneering role in brain mapping. With the aid of hitherto unpublished documents and figures, he explains the concepts behind Brodmann’s cytoarchitectonic maps and considers their impact on current neuroimaging approaches.}, 
